{"conjecture": "EJ = KP_y (segment E–J equals segment K–P_y). Equivalently EJ = KP_y = FP_y = FP_x^2/FV.", "reason": "Put j on the x-axis with F=(0,0) and the center A=(0,r). j is the tangent at F, since j ∥ f ⟂ GF. Let V=(v,0). Because GF is a diameter, angle FED = 90°, so V, the meeting point of the tangents at F and E, is the midpoint of the hypotenuse FD. Hence VF = VE = VD and D=(2v,0); directly, line GE has slope −r/v and meets y=0 at x=2v. Then e is x=2v and h1 is x=v. For P_x=(v,t), the ray FP_x hits e at K=(2v,2t)=2P_x. So P_x is the midpoint of FK, and m is the perpendicular bisector of FK, which gives P_yF = P_yK. Solving P_y·P_x = |P_x|^2 with y=2t gives P_y=((v^2−t^2)/v, 2t). Therefore KP_y = FP_y = (v^2+t^2)/|v| = FP_x^2/FV, which is the mean proportional FP_x^2 = FV·FP_y. H is the foot of P_y on j and D is the foot of K on j (K lies on e ⟂ j at D), so KP_y = HD. Triangle VDE is isosceles (VD=VE), and HJ ∥ DE, so triangle VHJ is similar to it and VH = VJ. Then EJ = |VJ − VE| = |VH − VD| = HD = (v^2+t^2)/|v|. Hence EJ = HD = KP_y = FP_y = FP_x^2/FV for every P_x on h1. Numerical check: EJ^2 ≈ 128.71 and KP_y^2 ≈ 128.71; also FP_x^2 ≈ 26.20 and FV·FP_y ≈ 2.309·11.345 ≈ 26.20.", "closes_goal": true}
```

